TreeSet: [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]

9. Custom Sorting Example
TreeSet<String> ts = new TreeSet<>(Comparator.reverseOrder());
ts.add("Hari");
ts.add("Ajay");
ts.add("Kiran");

System.out.println(ts);


Output:

[Kiran, Hari, Ajay]

